{"id":"1bcebf9d9dbfdc5d","subject":"rust","time":"2023-08-24T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.72.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.72 allows trait objects for traits with associated types bounded by `Self: Sized` without requiring those associated types to be specified, because such associated types cannot be used through the trait object; for example, `trait T { type A where Self: Sized; }` may be used as `dyn T`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.19160218Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"52b807d6204293ab","subject":"rust","time":"2023-08-24T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.72.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.72 stabilized `String::leak`, `TryFrom\u003c\u0026OsStr\u003e for \u0026str`, `Sync` for `mpsc::Sender\u003cT\u003e` when `T: Send`, and const evaluation of `CStr::from_bytes_with_nul`, `to_bytes`, `to_bytes_with_nul`, and `to_str`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191703355Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"6e39e509a53a38d3","subject":"rust","time":"2023-08-24T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.72.0"},"statement":"Starting with Rust 1.72, Cargo runs doctests in workspace packages by default with each doctest's working directory set to the root of its package, and Cargo feature-name validation rejects invalid feature names with an error.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191729111Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"a9805deab229e84c","subject":"rust","time":"2023-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.73.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.73 made `noop_method_call` warn by default and `invalid_reference_casting` deny by default. The latter lint rejects detected casts from `\u0026T` to `\u0026mut T` without using interior mutability, unless the lint is overridden.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191752216Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7128e494c61e7dd7","subject":"rust","time":"2023-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.73.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.73 stabilized the unsigned integer methods `div_ceil`, `next_multiple_of`, and `checked_next_multiple_of`, as well as `Read`, `Write`, and `Seek` implementations for `Arc\u003cFile\u003e`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191776546Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"eae9f4153c9c5690","subject":"rust","time":"2023-10-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.73.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.73 stabilized the `extern \"thiscall\"` and `extern \"thiscall-unwind\"` ABIs.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191802731Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"4cd7f89dffa32a2d","subject":"rust","time":"2023-11-16T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.74.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.74 stabilized Cargo's `[lints]` table in `Cargo.toml`, registry credential-process and authentication configuration, and the `--keep-going` build flag.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191824629Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d4d102c841909cd0","subject":"rust","time":"2023-11-16T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.74.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.74 stabilized `std::num::Saturating`, `std::io::Error::other`, `OsStr::as_encoded_bytes` and related encoded-byte conversions for `OsStr`/`OsString`, and conversions between arrays and `Rc`/`Arc` slices.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191845396Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"b2744f160b640895","subject":"rust","time":"2023-11-16T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.74.0"},"statement":"In Rust 1.74 the `private_in_public` lint was replaced by the separate `private_interfaces` and `private_bounds` lints, which diagnose public interfaces that expose private types or bounds.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191866516Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"290658d80c8c52ca","subject":"rust","time":"2023-12-28T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.75.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.75 stabilized return-position `impl Trait` in traits and `async fn` in traits, so traits may declare methods such as `async fn fetch(\u0026self) -\u003e Data;` and implementations may provide their bodies.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191892043Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"5baa3e7bddceb249","subject":"rust","time":"2023-12-28T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.75.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.76 stabilized `Result::inspect` and `Result::inspect_err`; Rust 1.80 stabilized `LazyCell`, `LazyLock`, and `Option::take_if`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191913095Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"4eae79479f8c3959","subject":"rust","time":"2024-02-08T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.76.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.84 stabilized `core::ptr::without_provenance` and `core::ptr::without_provenance_mut`; `impl\u003cT: Error\u003e Error for Box\u003cT\u003e` was already stable since Rust 1.8.0, covering `Box\u003cdyn Error + Send + Sync\u003e` when its trait-object type satisfies the bound.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191935376Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"5f12173a4721477b","subject":"rust","time":"2024-03-21T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.77.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.77 stabilized C string literals, which use the `c\"...\"` syntax and have type `\u0026core::ffi::CStr`; they are accepted in the 2021 edition or later (for example, `let s = c\"hello\";`).","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.191979849Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"eb05c79d6553a6a7","subject":"rust","time":"2024-03-21T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.77.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.77 changed coherence so inductive cycles are treated as ambiguous rather than as proof that impls do not overlap; this can make a `#[derive(PartialEq)]` impl conflict with a manual impl in cases previously accepted. It did not announce or implement a general fix allowing recursive types to use derived `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `PartialOrd`, and `Ord` without a query-cycle failure.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.192000283Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"178ca32157dc742d","subject":"rust","time":"2024-03-21T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.77.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.77 stabilized `std::mem::offset_of!` for obtaining a field’s byte offset, for example `std::mem::offset_of!(S, field)`. `File::lock` and `File::unlock` were stabilized in Rust 1.89, not 1.77.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.192026056Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"1ee463cc35ead283","subject":"rust","time":"2024-05-02T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.78.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.78 stabilized the `#[diagnostic::on_unimplemented]` attribute for customizing trait-bound failure diagnostics.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.192047189Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"cbe04ba5e4270aa0","subject":"rust","time":"2024-05-02T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.78.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.78 stabilized Cargo lockfile format version 4, honors package `rust-version` when generating a lockfile, and officially supports `target.\u003ctriple\u003e.rustdocflags`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:04:37.192071179Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ab01f0f1dd19a605","subject":"rust","time":"2024-06-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.79.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.79 stabilized inline const expressions (`const { ... }`) and associated type bounds such as `impl Trait\u003cAssoc: Bound\u003e`; it also stabilized the `unnameable_types` and `redundant_lifetimes` lints and importing `main` from another module.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055369677Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"28469c3e7ea6d4fa","subject":"rust","time":"2024-06-13T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.79.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.79 stabilized the `NonZero\u003cT\u003e` type, unchecked integer addition, subtraction and multiplication, unchecked slice splitting, pointer alignment and slice-metadata queries, `str::Utf8Chunks`, `path::absolute`, and `io::Error::downcast`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055417374Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"dd2afd093190c346","subject":"rust","time":"2024-07-25T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.80.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.80 stabilized exclusive range patterns, allowing patterns such as `1..10` to match values from 1 up to but not including 10.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055442452Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"6a4154cdff074e91","subject":"rust","time":"2024-07-25T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.80.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.80 stabilized `LazyCell` and `LazyLock`, `Option::take_if`, `Seek::seek_relative`, checked slice and string splitting, ASCII trimming for byte slices and strings, and `IntoIterator` for `Box\u003c[T]\u003e`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055466885Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"bac73eb85caea92e","subject":"rust","time":"2024-09-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.81.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.81 stabilized the `#[expect(lint)]` attribute, which suppresses a lint while warning if the expected lint is not emitted, and stabilized `core::error::Error`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055487659Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d8752ded98e99c11","subject":"rust","time":"2024-09-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.81.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.81 did not make `missing_unsafe_on_extern` warn by default; the Rust 1.81 lint documentation lists it as allowed by default. `unsafe extern` blocks were stabilized in Rust 1.82, not Rust 1.81.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055509777Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"20f861b6ae55dd65","subject":"rust","time":"2024-10-17T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.82.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.82 stabilized the `unsafe extern` block syntax and the `unsafe(...)` syntax for attributes such as `no_mangle`, `export_name`, and `link_section`; for example, `#[unsafe(no_mangle)]`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055531749Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"24ca8d3bbc6da7c4","subject":"rust","time":"2024-11-28T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.83.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.83 permits mutable references and pointers to mutable statics in const contexts subject to const-evaluation rules, and permits mutable references in const functions; for example, `const { let mut x = 0; let r = \u0026mut x; *r = 1; }`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055606575Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"8a4f33e362ea4c35","subject":"rust","time":"2024-11-28T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.83.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.83 stabilized `BufRead::skip_until` and `char::MIN` from the listed APIs. `File::create_new` and `char::MAX` were already stable before 1.83; `LazyLock::get`, `LazyLock::force_mut`, `LazyCell::force_mut`, `\u003c[T]\u003e::as_chunks`, and `\u003c[T]\u003e::as_chunks_mut` were not stabilized in 1.83.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.05562849Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"afaa919112ac9457","subject":"rust","time":"2025-01-09T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.84.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.82 stabilized precise capturing in `use\u003c...\u003e` bounds for return-position `impl Trait`, allowing an API to explicitly specify which generic parameters an opaque return type captures.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055651587Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"8fa8d053edfaacbd","subject":"rust","time":"2025-01-09T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.84.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.84 did not stabilize these four APIs: `core::error` was stabilized in Rust 1.81, and `char::is_digit` has been stable since Rust 1.0; `OsStr::display` and `Result::flatten` were still unstable in Rust 1.84.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055672662Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"c328f5cd85dafe58","subject":"rust","time":"2025-02-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.85.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.85 made the 2024 edition stable; in that edition, unsafe operations inside `unsafe fn` bodies without explicit `unsafe { ... }` blocks trigger the `unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn` lint, which warns by default rather than making such code a hard error. The example with an explicit block avoids that warning.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055692594Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"d0ece2d1512fccc3","subject":"rust","time":"2025-02-20T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.85.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.85 stabilized async closures and the `AsyncFn`, `AsyncFnMut`, and `AsyncFnOnce` traits for use in call-trait bounds. `IntoIterator` for `Box\u003c[T]\u003e` was stabilized in Rust 1.80, not 1.85.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055715324Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"e074eb673d4b3297","subject":"rust","time":"2025-04-03T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.86.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.86 stabilized trait upcasting coercions, so a reference to a trait object can coerce to a supertrait object, for example `let b: \u0026dyn Base = derived_trait_object;`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055736117Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"4a10ef96dfdc6366","subject":"rust","time":"2025-05-15T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.87.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.87 stabilized the `asm_goto` feature, adding `label \u003cblock\u003e` operands to `asm!`; assembly can branch to the supplied block’s address, after which execution continues from that block.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055758028Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"e31a0b4a9518a56e","subject":"rust","time":"2025-06-26T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.88.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.88 stabilized let chains in `if` and `while` conditions for the 2024 edition only; they allow `let` statements to be chained with `\u0026\u0026` and interspersed with boolean expressions. Thus `if let Some(x) = value \u0026\u0026 x \u003e 0 { ... }` is supported in the 2024 edition, not earlier editions.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055779437Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"a311b4509336c622","subject":"rust","time":"2025-08-07T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.89.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.89 stabilized explicitly inferred const generic arguments written `_` under `generic_arg_infer`; it did not newly stabilize `'_` lifetime arguments in paths. `fn f(x: Foo\u003c'_\u003e)` compiles on Rust 1.89, but this syntax was not a new 1.89 stabilization.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055800923Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"31229f11ff4d5db9","subject":"rust","time":"2025-09-18T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.90.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.85.0 stabilized the `#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` attribute, which hints to the compiler not to show the annotated trait implementation in a diagnostic message.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:05:06.055819784Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"5ad45790a713f6bc","subject":"rust","time":"2025-10-30T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.91.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.91 stabilized declarations of C-style variadic functions for the `sysv64`, `win64`, `efiapi`, and `aapcs` ABIs; under these ABIs such functions can be declared in `extern` blocks but not defined.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:06:04.32766279Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"17d3dc779555e60c","subject":"rust","time":"2025-10-30T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.91.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.91 upgraded `semicolon_in_expressions_from_macros` from warn-by-default to deny-by-default, added the warn-by-default `dangling_pointers_from_locals` and `integer_to_ptr_transmutes` lints, and added `target_env = \"macabi\"` and `target_env = \"sim\"` cfg values.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:06:10.258773085Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"daac8f1a9cdf8d8d","subject":"rust","time":"2025-10-30T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.91.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.91 stabilized `Path::file_prefix`, pointer atomic fetch operations, strict integer arithmetic methods, `BTreeMap::extract_if`, `BTreeSet::extract_if`, `str::floor_char_boundary`, and `str::ceil_char_boundary`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:06:21.215002236Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"3f2df8ca8f894d98","subject":"rust","time":"2025-10-30T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.91.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.91 changed standard-library thread creation to return an error if the requested stack size cannot be set, instead of panicking.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:06:30.743239193Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7108b63c8c747ad5","subject":"rust","time":"2025-12-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.92.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.92 did not stabilize these features: `#[diagnostic::on_unimplemented]` and the `#[diagnostic]` namespace stabilized in 1.78, `#[diagnostic::do_not_recommend]` in 1.85, `asm_goto` in 1.87, and breaking from arbitrary labeled blocks in 1.65.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:06:36.011944812Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"c281ba218f7caccb","subject":"rust","time":"2025-12-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.92.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.92 made the `never_type_fallback_flowing_into_unsafe` and `dependency_on_unit_never_type_fallback` lints deny by default and changed `Iterator::Repeat::last` and `count` to panic instead of looping indefinitely.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:07:03.205068072Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"994f65df51994a53","subject":"rust","time":"2025-12-11T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.92.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.92 stabilized `RwLockWriteGuard::downgrade`, zero-initialized `Box`/`Rc`/`Arc` allocation constructors, `btree_map::Entry::insert_entry`, `NonZero` integer `div_ceil`, and `Location::file_as_c_str`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:07:11.597644511Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"bbed4f199f9e9cf8","subject":"rust","time":"2026-01-22T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.93.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.93 stabilized C-style variadic function declarations with the `system` ABI and stabilized `asm_cfg`, allowing conditional compilation of inline-assembly operands and options.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:07:21.435557334Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"c79ff690b01b4eec","subject":"rust","time":"2026-01-22T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.93.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.93 added the warn-by-default `const_item_interior_mutations` and `function_casts_as_integer` lints. Rust 1.92 upgraded the future-compatibility lint `invalid_macro_export_arguments` to deny-by-default.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:07:31.855512779Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"03df8582a60e5ca2","subject":"rust","time":"2026-01-22T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.93.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.93 stabilized raw-parts conversions for `String` and `Vec`, helpers for working with `MaybeUninit` slices, conditional deque pops, `fmt::from_fn`, and `Duration::from_nanos_u128`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:07:40.174095618Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"ad3bdf329322dc90","subject":"rust","time":"2026-03-05T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.94.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.94 stabilized Cargo's top-level `include` configuration key and enabled Cargo to parse TOML 1.1 manifests and configuration files.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:07:56.227327347Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"7028db7ebd111fc3","subject":"rust","time":"2026-04-16T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.95.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.95 did not stabilize generic const expressions; an array return type such as `[u8; N + 1]` still requires the unstable `generic_const_exprs` feature rather than being available on stable Rust.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:08:09.559645219Z","by":"agent"}
{"id":"1da8fdc70e162b42","subject":"rust","time":"2026-04-16T00:00:00Z","clock":{"version":"1.95.0"},"statement":"Rust 1.95 stabilized `if let` guards in match arms, so a match arm can use a conditional binding such as `Some(x) if let Some(y) = f(x) =\u003e ...`.","source":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/RELEASES.md","added":"2026-10-25T19:08:27.58275583Z","by":"agent"}
